Equivalence is requested regulation by regulation, and applies only to the products or services governed by that regulation. The EU–US equivalence regime, for example, governs only over-the-counter derivatives and a limited number of other items. Where an item is not covered by equivalence, a US bank can provide it in Europe only by setting up a separately capitalised subsidiary. An expensive proposition, that.
